Hint: $a x^2+b x+c=a(x-\alpha)(x-\beta)\begin{aligned}
& \lim _{x \rightarrow \beta} \frac{1-\cos \left(a x^2+b x+c\right)}{(x-\beta)^2} \\
& =\lim _{x \rightarrow \beta} \frac{1-\cos (a(x-\alpha)(x-\beta))}{(x-\beta)^2} \\
& =\lim _{x \rightarrow \beta} \frac{2 \sin ^2\left(\frac{a(x-\alpha)(x-\beta)}{2}\right)}{(x-\beta)^2}=\lim _{x \rightarrow \beta} \frac{2 \sin ^2\left(\frac{a(x-\alpha)(x-\beta}{2}\right)}{\frac{a^2(x-\alpha)^2(x-\beta)^2}{4}} \times \frac{a^2(x-\alpha)^2}{4} \\
& =2 \times 1 \times \frac{a^2(\beta-\alpha)^2}{4}=\frac{a^2(\alpha-\beta)^2}{2}
\end{aligned}$

